BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Falsettos
DTSTART:20260823T190000
DTEND:20260823T220000
DTSTAMP:20260823T114110Z
UID:8c37bc1cd8cddade9b97531473024a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Hilarious\, heartbreaking\, and utterly unique\, Falsettos is 
 a contemporary musical set in the late 1970s\, exploring love and its cons
 equences. When Marvin leaves his wife and son to be with his lover\, their
  world is upended\, but amidst the chaos\, new bonds form and redefine wha
 t family can be. Falsettos is a tribute to the messy and beautiful connect
 ions that hold us together —through baseball games\, bar mitzvahs\, and 
 the unexpected twists of life\, requiring everyone to learn to grow up and
  face their future with love and dignity. This show will be running from 8
 /13-23 at Main Street Landing's Blackbox Theater with showtimes as follows
 : 7 PM: 8/13\, 14\, 15\, 20\, 21\, 22 1 PM: 8/15\, 16\, 22\, 23\n\nSources
 : Vermont Public
LOCATION:Main Street Landing Blackbox\, 60 Lake Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/falsettos-
 21-07-2026-14-18-35
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury: LADAMA
DTSTART:20260823T170000
DTEND:20260823T190000
DTSTAMP:20260823T114110Z
UID:516e34fcc7161d403c9bc18f0e30f2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Catamount Arts welcomes NPR Tiny Desk darlings LADAMA to Dog M
 ountain\, Sunday\, August 23rd\, as part of the Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury M
 usic Series. Reinvigorating traditional Latin sounds from across the Ameri
 cas with a boundless enthusiasm and tantalizing joy\, LADAMA’s show star
 ts at 5pm. Comprised of virtuosic musicians\, composers\, and educators La
 ra Klaus\, Daniela Serna and Mafer Bandola\, LADAMA are sisters in song an
 d spirit. Harnessing music from Brazil\, Columbia\, and Venezuela\, their 
 respective countries of origin\, the group utilizes traditional and non-tr
 aditional instruments to create a rich Latin Alternative sound that blends
  folkloric forms with a modern twist. Their music has been described by NP
 R as having “irresistible spirit and universal appeal.” LADAMA met on 
 the road in 2014 while touring Los Angeles\, Arizona\, and New Mexico as p
 art of the prestigious OneBeat Program. Between individual performances\, 
 leading youth workshops and public music-making events\, Lara\, Daniela an
 d Mafer uncovered a common dream of building communities through sound and
  empowering women and youth through music. LADAMA delivers an utterly uniq
 ue experience as they flow from the electric to the acoustic\, from Spanis
 h to English and Portuguese\, and from the high plains of Venezuela to the
  Colombian coast. Borders are meaningless as their sound transports audien
 ces to a future where the world communicates beyond continents and culture
 s through sound and story. Sunday’s LADAMA concert at Dog Mountain is fr
 ee and open to everyone—including dogs. Patrons are encouraged to bring 
 a blanket or a low beach chair\, sunscreen\, and water\, but leave the alc
 ohol at home. Beer\, wine\, and cocktails will be available for purchase a
 t the St. Johnsbury Distillery beer garden on site\; bringing alcohol from
  off-site is strictly prohibited. Patrons are welcome to pack a picnic din
 ner or bring cash to grab something from one of the food trucks\; there wi
 ll be at least two food options available for purchase at every Sunday con
 cert. Overflow parking is available at the Fairbanks Scales parking lot\, 
 where RCT will shuttle passengers up to Dog Mountain and back. New this ye
 ar\, RCT will begin shuttling folks from the St. Johnsbury Welcome Center 
 to Dog Mountain every Sunday at 4pm\, and then back to the Welcome Center 
 after the concert. Thanks to generous support from RCT\, shuttle service t
 o the concert venue is free of charge. In addition to monthly Sunday conce
 rts at Dog Mountain\, Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury hosts free concerts at Fina
 l Fridays block parties\, on the last Friday of June\, July\, and August\,
  in partnership with Downtown St. Johnsbury. For a full summer of free fam
 ily-friendly live music\, plan to be at Dog Mountain\, every Sunday\, at 5
 pm\, and don’t miss Final Fridays on Railroad Street! For more informati
 on\, including the full line-up of Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury Music Series a
 rtists\, visit www.catamountarts.org or email info@catamountarts.org. To l
 earn more about Final Fridays block parties\, featuring free family-friend
 ly activities in downtown St. Johnsbury including live music courtesy of L
 evitt AMP St. Johnsbury\, visit www.discoverstjohnsbury.org. The Levitt AM
 P St. Johnsbury Music Series is supported in part by the Levitt Family Fou
 ndation\, which exists to strengthen the social fabric of America. The Lev
 itt Family Foundation partners with communities to activate underused outd
 oor spaces\, creating welcoming inclusive destinations where the power of 
 free live music brings people together and invigorates community life. In 
 2026\, the Levitt Family Foundation is supporting over 1\,000 free concert
 s in 100+ towns and cities throughout the country\, bringing joy to over a
  million people. In addition to supporting free concerts\, the Levitt Foun
 dation is dedicated to advancing equitable music ecosystems through resear
 ch and partnerships. Learn more at www.levitt.org.\n\nSources: Vermont Pub
 lic
LOCATION:Dog Mountain\, 143 Parks Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/levitt-amp
 -st-johnsbury-ladama-18-08-2026-12-00-09
END:VEVENT
