BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music in the Meadow: Dan Tyminski Band
DTSTART:20260823T190000
DTEND:20260823T235900
DTSTAMP:20260823T114110Z
UID:0638c584d2f8eec1a3cd1dd4e07c53@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Throughout his 30+ year career\, Tyminski has left his mark in
  every corner of modern music. In recent years\, Tyminski’s live shows w
 ith the Dan Tyminski Band have become bluegrass fan favorites and are regu
 larly on the must-see lists among music fans of any genre. Dan has been ho
 nored with 14 Grammy Awards and is a four-time Male Vocalist of the Year h
 onoree by the International Bluegrass Music Association. His voice famousl
 y accompanies George Clooney’s performance of the Stanley Brothers’ cl
 assic song\, “I Am A Man of Constant Sorrow\,” in the film\, Oh Brothe
 r\, Where Art Thou? and his vocal collaboration with Swedish DJ Avicii on 
 the song “Hey Brother” was a global smash\, having been streamed more 
 than a billion times to date. His diverse solo projects and years of work 
 with Alison Krauss and Union Station have yielded troves of award-winning 
 music.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:von Trapp Family Lodge Concert Meadow\, 854 Trapp Hill Rd.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/music-in-t
 he-meadow-dan-tyminski-band-05-06-2026-09-26-57
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunday Classical: Duo Dolce
DTSTART:20260823T100000
DTEND:20260823T110000
DTSTAMP:20260823T114110Z
UID:b80084288d995a6bfd17df5a95da0e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Duo Dolce features Laura Markowitz on violin and John Dunlop o
 n cello. Both are members of the Vermont Symphony Orchestra and perform wi
 th ensembles including Eleva Chamber Players\, the Opera Company of Middle
 bury\, Cricket Blue\, and the Rhizome Quartet\, as well as alongside vocal
 ist Moira Smiley. John also performs with the TURN and Jukebox ensembles\,
  premiering cutting-edge contemporary music\, while Laura performs with Sy
 lvia\, a quartet dedicated to music by women composers. Their program will
  showcase an eclectic mix of baroque\, classical and modern repertoire and
  even a few Celtic and Swedish tunes. Bring your weekend to a brilliant cr
 escendo with Vermont’s finest classical players in the BCA Center galler
 y\, alongside our summer exhibitions\, Everything is Everything: Will Kass
 o Condry and Dream / Mộng : Veronica Pham. Summer in the City is made po
 ssible in part thanks to Underwriters at the Pomerleau Family Foundation\;
  Supporters Burlington Telecom\, Myti\, Soundtoys\, and Lake Champlain Cho
 colates\, and Community Partner American Flatbread Burlington & Mothership
  Brewery. Media Sponsors: Seven Days and WCAX.⁠\n\nSources: Vermont.com
 \, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Burlington City Arts\, Burlington\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/sunday-cla
 ssical-duo-dolce-31-05-2026-17-10-44
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Struggle: Anti-Empire Talks in the Paper Mâché Cathed
 ral
DTSTART:20260823T173000
DTEND:20260823T190000
DTSTAMP:20260823T114110Z
UID:355df6d81d4b221c9bbd16b99b88b1@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Bread & Puppet Press presents The Art of Resistance: Anti-Empi
 re Talks in the Paper Mâché Cathedral\, a summer speaker series explorin
 g empire\, capitalism\, war\, and resistance through lectures\, conversati
 ons\, and teach-ins. Held in Bread & Puppet's Paper Mâché Cathedral in G
 lover\, Vermont\, the series features Richard Wolff (remote) in conversati
 on with Quincy Saul on As US Empire Declines\, US Capitalism Does Too (Jul
 y 12--program starts with music at 3PM\, talk starts at 4PM)\, Greg Joly o
 n Scott Nearing's The Great Madness (July 19)\, Omar Dahi on Syria's destr
 uction (July 26)\, Susan Abulhawa in conversation with Corinna Mullin on W
 estern Imperialism and the Struggle for Palestinian National Liberation (A
 ugust 16)\, and Max Blumenthal on Occupied Government in Crisis (August 23
 ). Admission is $5\; no one turned away for lack of funds. Every week thro
 ugh Aug 23\, 2026.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Bread & Puppet Theater\, 753 Heights Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-art-of
 -struggle-anti-empire-talks-in-the-paper-mache-cathedral-01-07-2026-17-41-
 49
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twilight On the Tavern Lawn: The Stockwell Brothers
DTSTART:20260823T180000
DTEND:20260823T200000
DTSTAMP:20260823T114110Z
UID:7b4b68f8308c6324166f4d1f574783@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Bruce\, Barry\, and Alan Stockwell blend traditional and progr
 essive acoustic music with original singer/songwriter material\, inventive
  banjo work\, alternative rhythms\, and rich three-part harmonies. Featuri
 ng 2005 MerleFest Bluegrass Banjo Contest winner Bruce Stockwell\, the tri
 o has shared stages with legends including Bill Monroe\, Doc Watson\, Earl
  Scruggs\, Mary Chapin Carpenter\, Jonathan Edwards\, and Asleep at the Wh
 eel. They have recorded with Mike Auldridge and Phil Rosenthal of The Seld
 om Scene and have toured extensively throughout the United States\, Canada
 \, and Europe.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Putney Tavern Lawn\, 133 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/twilight-o
 n-the-tavern-lawn-the-stockwell-brothers-20-07-2026-21-33-18
END:VEVENT
